The strict `is False` check keeps legacy records (no "durable" key -> None) and all non-tuning handlers blocking exactly as today. Net behavior: persistable keys (best_of_n etc.) survive restart via the existing Settings override source (settings.py:104-126) and their APPLIED record keeps blocking (durable=True); non-persistable keys (auto_route/model_evolution) legitimately re-surface for approval after restart, and in-process re-proposal spam is prevented by RoutingReadiness's own live-flag check + _proposed guard (components.py:581-585). Add tests: handler-applied persistable tuning appears in load_overrides(data_dir) and survives a second Cortex on the same data_dir; a durable=False APPLIED record replayed from disk does not dedupe-block; a durable=True one still does.

In skyn3t/studio/visual_check.py, rewrite _explicit_vision_backend to mirror LLMClient._resolve_backend's auto arm using the cheap module-level seams (local import, same pattern as the existing `from skyn3t.adapters.llm import _no_mcp_args` at l.510):

def _explicit_vision_backend(settings: Any) -> str:
    backend = str(getattr(settings, "llm_backend", "auto") or "auto").strip().lower()
    if backend in {"openrouter", "claude_cli", "kimi_cli"}:
        return backend
    if backend != "auto":
        return ""
    from skyn3t.adapters.llm import LLMClient, _auto_priority_order, openrouter_key
    for provider in _auto_priority_order(settings):
        if LLMClient._cli_available(provider):
            return f"{provider}_cli" if provider in {"claude", "kimi"} else ""
    if bool(getattr(settings, "auto_allow_openrouter", False)) and openrouter_key(settings):
        return "openrouter"
    return ""

Design points: (1) vision follows codegen's RESOLUTION — if auto resolves to codex/copilot (no vision adapter) it returns "" and soft-skips rather than skipping past to a vision-capable CLI codegen didn't select; (2) the auto_allow_openrouter arm exactly mirrors _resolve_backend (llm.py:1969-1972) and the M15 router fix (model_router.py:850-854): opt-in is consent, a dormant key alone still never activates OpenRouter vision; (3) use classmethod LLMClient._cli_available + _auto_priority_order, never LLMClient(settings) (heavy __init__, breaks SimpleNamespace doubles) and never raw shutil.which (bypasses the suite's CLI fence); (4) _make_cli_vision_fn keeps its own shutil.which guard, so a stale availability cache degrades to None (soft-skip), never a crash. Also update the stale docstring in _explicit_vision_backend ("auto is Codex-only") and make_vision_fn/make_click_vision_fn's "auto never activates either" wording, plus the stale comment at skyn3t/config/settings.py:220-222 ("Automatic build execution always uses Codex CLI"). Add the three new tests named in fix_risk.

